3.3 Comprehensive Grammar Reference & Conjugation Tables
Pedagogical Function
Serves as the structural blueprint for the language. Users review this material prior to sentence synthesis and access it as contextual support during drills.
The 3x3 Core Verb Matrix Model
The central component of the grammar engine is a 3x3 structural matrix crossing Tense (Past, Present, Future) with Form (Affirmative, Negative, Interrogative).


Form / Tense
	Past Simple
	Present Simple
	Future Simple
	Affirmative (+)
	I worked / Я работал
	I work / Я работаю
	I will work / Я буду работать
	Negative (-)
	I did not work / Я не работал
	I do not work / Я не работаю
	I will not work / Я не буду работать
	Interrogative (?)
	Did I work? / Я работал?
	Do I work? / Я работаю?
	Will I work? / Я буду работать?
	Structural Rule Specifications
* Auxiliary Automation: Explicitly highlights operational shifts in auxiliary verbs (did, do, does, will).
* Pronoun Alignment: Integrated person/number reference tables (I, You, He, She, It, We, They) detailing suffix alterations and agreement rules.
* Contextual Pairings: Side-by-side bilingual examples detailing common usage edge cases.


