3.4 Interactive Practice: Sentence Translation & Unscrambling
Objective
Transition from passive recognition to active production by enforcing syntactically correct sentence assembly from randomized word pools.
Interface Layout
* Source Prompt Area: Displays source sentence to translate (e.g., "Ты пойдёшь завтра в кино?").
* Assembly Bay: Target area where selected word tiles snap into sequential order.
* Tile Pool (Word Bank): Scrambled array of target-language tiles containing correct sentence tokens plus 1–2 distractor tokens.


+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Prompt: "Ты пойдёшь завтра в кино?"                               |
|                                                                   |
|  Assembly Bay:                                                    |
|  [ Will ]  [ you ]  [ go ]  [ to ]  [ ... ]                       |
|                                                                   |
|  Tile Pool:                                                       |
|  [ the ]   [ go ]   [ tomorrow ]   [ cinema ]   [ went ]  [ ? ]   |
|                                                                   |
|  [ CHECK ANSWER ]                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
Workflow & Behavioral Logic
1. Tile Placement: Tapping an available tile in the pool moves it to the next open position in the Assembly Bay.
2. Tile Removal: Tapping a tile within the Assembly Bay returns it to the Tile Pool pool.
3. Evaluation: Pressing Check Answer locks the UI state and validates the array sequence against target string definitions.
4. Error Handling: If an incorrect sequence is submitted, the engine highlights misplaced tokens, reveals the target structure, and provides a direct link to the associated grammar rule.


