4. UI/UX Design System & Behavioral Rules
Color Palette & Design Tokens
The visual design utilizes a slate-neutral base paired with high-contrast structural accents to minimize fatigue and support long learning sessions.


* Neutral Slate: #0F172A (Text/Headers), #64748B (Secondary UI), #F8FAFC (Surface Background).
* Success Emerald: #10B981 (Correct State, Mastery Indicators).
* Error Coral: #EF4444 (Incorrect State, Alert Triggers).
* Accent Indigo: #6366F1 (Active Elements, Focus Ring, Primary Buttons).
Ergonomics & Adaptability
* Touch Targets: All interactive components (word tiles, options, buttons) maintain a minimum target area of 48dp x 48dp.
* Viewport Handling: Optimized for primary single-handed vertical mobile usage while dynamically scaling to multi-column desktop layouts.


